# Signing material must never enter this repo, even by accident. Tundra's update chain is a
# single CA with an offline root, and a leak of either key is unrecoverable: every installed
# machine trusts them, and RAUC has no rotation mechanism to fall back on.
#
# This is the mechanical backstop for a stray `git add -A`. Staging explicitly is still the
# rule, and this list is not a substitute for it.
*.pem
*.key
*.rsa
*.priv
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cer
*.crt
*.gpg
*.asc
.env
.env.*

# Build and image output. This repo holds configuration; images belong to Phase 2.
*.img
*.iso
*.raucb
*.apk

# RPM leaves these beside a `%config(noreplace)` file it wanted to update. They carry the
# packager's version of a file the apply script has modified, which is useful on the pilot and
# meaningless in the tree.
*.rpmnew
*.rpmsave
*.rpmorig

# Scratch output from the lint harness: the BusyBox applet list pulled out of the Alpine
# container, and anything else written while a check runs.
.lint-cache/

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
